(7195710, 1072862, 23439, '<td valign="top">"I truly don''t understand those who get so obsessed with video games that they neglect living their lives"<br/> <br/>Just came across this, after seeing your The Reader, The Listener and the Daydreamer image. As an avid gamer, I think video games get this view from non gamers too often. And while being obsessed with anything to the point you neglect other aspects of your life isn''t healthy, this also applies to TV, reading and even photography. How you described reading, is exactly what games are to many people. The stories told in some games now easily match the best I''ve read in a book or seen in a movie. In some ways even surpassing those mediums because you''re playing an active role in that story being told.</td>', '"I truly don''t understand those who get so obsessed with video games that they neglect living their lives" Just came across this, after seeing your The Reader, The Listener and the Daydreamer image. As an avid gamer, I think video games get this view from non gamers too often. And while being obsessed with anything to the point you neglect other aspects of your life isn''t healthy, this also applies to TV, reading and even photography. How you described reading, is exactly what games are to many people. The stories told in some games now easily match the best I''ve read in a book or seen in a movie. In some ways even surpassing those mediums because you''re playing an active role in that story being told.', '2014-03-30 07:59:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7224793, 1072810, 116247, '<td valign="top">Such an addicting game!!</td>', 'Such an addicting game!!', '2014-06-05 00:14:40.000000', NULL, 0),
